**Tips to Get Writers, Agencies and Clients on the Same Page**

In the last few days I have had several conversations with Content
Marketing Agencies about how to get everyone involved in the content
creation process aligned on what is acceptable use of AI.

They all reported the same thing... Clients expect Original content! But
what "original" content is had different definitions.  

This email includes several tips for getting writers, agencies and
clients all on the same page to allow for the efficient creation of AI
free content that doesn't bog you down with an inefficient process...

**Key Tips:**

* Not implementing any AI detection process for your content team is by
default accepting the use of it... The good news is you are using
Originality.AI and will therefore win business away from an
agency/writer that is putting their head in the sand and pretending like
AI content doesn't exist because their clients are not asking about it
(yet)!

* Communicating your stance and procedure for detecting the use of AI in
content is key for everyone involved. Letting your writers or
clients know that you are using Originality helps avoid future
questions. 

* It is best to avoid implementing a HARD target detection number vs
tracking numbers for all work submitted and making decisions on the
average results. It is better to look at 10 submitted articles and aim
at an average of 75% Original while investigating (using our chrome
extension) any articles that have a greater then 50% chance of being AI
generated. Requiring EVERY article to be above a certain Originality.AI
threshold can lead to a lot of potentially unnecessary edits. 

* If possible have writers create their content in a Google document
that they share edit access and you can use our free Chrome Extension to
resolve any potential false positives.

* Formatting changes can change the score. If you think the "same"
document gets different results copy the text from the share report link
for the different scans and compare in our free Text Compare tool
<https://jonhaver.lt.acemlnb.com/Prod/link-tracker?redirectUrl=aHR0cHMlM0ElMkYlMkZvcmlnaW5hbGl0eS5haSUyRnRleHQtY29tcGFyZSUyRg==&sig=2BkktsxCGA4wHdhfMJRwjq5SyrxAzNtEBtt8XKAji4L3&iat=1683832357&a=%7C%7C798597961%7C%7C&account=jonhaver%2Eactivehosted%2Ecom&email=v46NNu9ecA6QT5ACtUmNztrY6RruV%2F%2FREdQz1g%2F7A3RC4V%2BSN8YpK6daWp8%3D%3A%2F12nzRWdHcjBSpiyxpZnujj8R%2FogQbX4&s=c2aa77b6f0a29bb9a1c1a13f88329783&i=1823A1987A61A28328>.

* We have yet to speak to a content marketing team that didn't have at
least one writer using AI

* AI editing will show up as AI generated... it has to otherwise someone
could have AI "edit" an article so that it passes plagiarism and then
there would be no controls to stop them from passing it off as their
own. 

* Originality.AI is the ONLY tool on the market that can detect if
Quillbot or another paraphrasing tool has been used. 

Check for AI at Originality.AI <https://jonhaver.lt.acemlnb.com/Prod/link-tracker?redirectUrl=aHR0cHMlM0ElMkYlMkZvcmlnaW5hbGl0eS5haSUyRg==&sig=Bq34DuU9MDSdnB1VcXGFVJZyhFULG5zE9VJXaCmUYPZ8&iat=1683832357&a=%7C%7C798597961%7C%7C&account=jonhaver%2Eactivehosted%2Ecom&email=v46NNu9ecA6QT5ACtUmNztrY6RruV%2F%2FREdQz1g%2F7A3RC4V%2BSN8YpK6daWp8%3D%3A%2F12nzRWdHcjBSpiyxpZnujj8R%2FogQbX4&s=c2aa77b6f0a29bb9a1c1a13f88329783&i=1823A1987A61A28325>

